			<div class="content" id="post-content-3612452">
									

<p>Seems genuine and heartful (I presume), but it's not too interesting. You give us a concept and idea, and tease at what it could be, but you stop short of bothering to explore it at all and instead just prop it up with the unconventional take of it being connected to otherkin. I mean, the way you wrote it has already made it much more genuine than the other article we have on otherkin but at the same time that's really the only major draw to this article, and that doesn't really count as a draw.</p>
<p>I wanna know more about this place, why it manifests the way it does, get sucked into its world, and there's nothing there. This isn't the sort of &quot;Oooh, I love what went into this and I <em>have to know more</em>&quot;, it's &quot;Oh, that's it&quot;?. I know that you have Carling there to try and give us more information, but that's not a substitute for showing. It was still written well and kind enough that I'm not gonna downvote; I just think you leave off way too much potential here to really earn an upvote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
