														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4192507">
									

<p>I'm conflicted. As a lifelong Tolkien fan, the idea of stepping on the Straight Way and journeying to Elvenhome is something out of a daydream. But it seems far too straightforward and&#8230; benign for something set in the Foundation Universe.</p>
<p>It kills me to say it, but I think it would be better if there were multiple Exploration Logs, with each one being *radically* different depending on the personal tastes of the -A (someone who loves Narnia sees talking animals on the walls and hears a lion's roar; someone who loves Peter Pan sees Neverland, etc.), and the implication that whatever it really is, it's not any of those things at the end.</p>
<p>Alternatively, the Foundation could be their classic, overcontrolling self and try to fuck with the Faeries, resulting in a horrifying, and classically Fae, response, in which the city becomes hostile.</p>
<p>As it is, it's too noblebright for the foundation. No vote though; I couldn't bring myself to downvote something out of Tolkien.</p>

